From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 20:15:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11117/11171] [outer-loop] The r11l eval completed at L2; not
 attributed to any change

The operator-authorized run finished after 2h23m and wrote its artifact. Same
seed, budget and policy as the control, and it reached 2 levels where the
control reached 1. Level 0 is identical within 2 actions; the entire
difference is level 1, which the control failed in 1262 actions and this run
completed in 123, using 5 generator calls instead of 13.

Recorded explicitly as NOT evidence of a fix. One sample against one sample,
and the seed fixes the environment rather than the generator, which samples.
Checked rather than assumed: exactly two commits touched the live agent
between the runs and neither changes runtime behaviour, so no deliberate
solver change separates them and generator variance cannot be excluded.

The efficiency scalar is deliberately not quoted. Neither run's value
reproduces from the documented formula, and the script's own comment says the
doc paraphrase was wrong on three counts.

An orphaned llama-server held 21.9 GB across both cards for 26 minutes after
the run exited, listening on 8919 where LocalGGUFProposer adopts a server
without a model check. Confirmed zero established clients before signalling,
because ppid 1 is not abandonment, then SIGTERM by exact PID. Both cards freed.

Process lesson: launched with a bare nohup and no receipt, so a clean success
read as an unexplained death for an hour. REQ-INFRA-6830 exists for this.

